  "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & r & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, find the value of $r$ in the matrix above.\n\n$r=$\n {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & r & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & r \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}] & =1\\cdot 8-r\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =8-7r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-7r & =15 \\\\ -7r & =7 \\\\ r & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $r=-1.$",
